<div className={"prose font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant space-y-4 leading-relaxed"}>
<p>{"\n              Perched at an exhilarating 1,850 meters above sea level in the serene heights of Faraya Mzaar, Cedar Peak Stone Chalet is an architectural tribute to the timeless alpine traditions of Mount Lebanon. Hand-chiseled local limestone walls up to 40 centimeters thick provide whisper-quiet insulation and authentic rustic mountain elegance.\n            "}</p>
<p>{"\n              Step inside to soaring ceilings framed by fragrant Lebanese cedar timber beams, centering on a monumental handcrafted stone chimney fireplace. The open-plan living hall is tailored for memorable winter gatherings, furnished with deep lounge seating, handwoven local textiles, and floor-to-ceiling glass framing unobstructed sunsets that turn the mountain ridges crimson and violet.\n            "}</p>
<p>{"\n              After a long day carving the slopes of Mzaar, soak in the private heated outdoor hydrotherapy spa under crisp starry skies, or gather around the artisanal copper fondue table for an intimate alpine dinner. Every detail has been curated to merge deep Mediterranean warmth with five-star mountain comfort.\n            "}</p>
</div>
</section>

